    "body": "No, per discussion with CSP folks, header-initiated fetches are not generally governed by CSP at all. The reasoning is that CSP is a mechanism for protection against HTML injection defense, not header-injection defense; if an attacker can inject headers, then they can mess up your CSP and do all sorts of bad things.\r\n\r\nI guess `Link` might be governed by CSP, but that's more of a historical accident...",
    "created_at": "2025-09-24T06:28:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-24T06:28:06Z",
